{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:22045-1","published":"2026-10-07T09:41:30Z","modified":"2026-10-19T17:23:11.652739743Z","related":["CVE-2025-1218","CVE-2025-14181","CVE-2026-6103","CVE-2026-91765","CVE-2026-91766","CVE-2026-91767","CVE-2026-91768","CVE-2026-91769","CVE-2026-92842","CVE-2026-93682"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-1218","CVE-2025-14181","CVE-2026-6103","CVE-2026-91765","CVE-2026-91766","CVE-2026-91767","CVE-2026-91768","CVE-2026-91769","CVE-2026-92842","CVE-2026-93682"],"summary":"Security update for php8","details":"This update for php8 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-1218: php: php: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read in mysqlnd wire protocol parser (bsc#1282981).\n- CVE-2025-14181: Integer overflow to buffer overflow in soap HTTP parsing (bsc#1283216).\n- CVE-2026-6103: Archive entry injection via integer overflow in TAR parser (bsc#1282980).\n- CVE-2026-91765: Denial of Service via unbounded recursion in SOAP parser (bsc#1282875).\n- CVE-2026-91766: Credential disclosure via cross-origin HTTP redirects (bsc#1282876).\n- CVE-2026-91767: Information disclosure via crafted TLS server certificate (bsc#1282877).\n- CVE-2026-91768: Access control bypass via partial IPv6 address comparison (bsc#1282878).\n- CVE-2026-91769: OpenSSL stream peer verification falls back to the Common Name whenever no `subjectAltName` matches,\n  allowing trusted certificate impersonation (bsc#1283044).\n- CVE-2026-92842: Information disclosure via out-of-bounds read in stream filters (bsc#1282985).\n- CVE-2026-93682: Out-of-bounds read via empty HTTP redirect Location header (bsc#1282986).\n\nChanges for php8:\n\n- Updated to version 8.4.26\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"apache2-mod_php8","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/apache2-mod_php8&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.4.26-160000.1.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"apache2-mod_php8":"8.4.26-160